# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — execution log

- P18-V01 inherited-trait correction: the pinned Java 5.5.1
  `TopicValidator.ValidateResult` does not declare `equals` or `hashCode`;
  reflection resolves both methods to `java.lang.Object`. Java self-equality is
  true, while two separately constructed results with the same fields compare
  unequal. Rust had derived structural `PartialEq`/`Eq`, adding value equality
  that Java does not provide. Removed those trait implementations and added a
  compile-fail rustdoc guard.
- Extended `TopicValidatorFixtures` with Java reflection and identity cases;
  updated the invoked fixture and Rust differential. Fixture SHA-256:
  `5f6b913ce7174c578fe069cd3d1b6badb44c971b8c16c164378ab6129dc23c55`.
- Updated the Phase 6 API map, requirement audit, and release checklist. This
  closes one inherited-trait discrepancy only; broad P18-V01 remains open.
- Verification passed: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-features
  --locked` (21 unit tests, 19 message-decoder integration tests, the Topic
  Validator differential, and 15 doctests); `cargo clippy -p
  rocketmq-classic-common --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`;
  `mvn -q -o -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 scenarios, fixture
  drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes); `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; and
  `git diff --check`.
- The full workspace P18-V02 gate still needs rerunning on the revision that
  includes this correction.
